    Chief Ines Calder: Tea's over. Gather round. Two minutes, then the board.
    Chief Ines Calder: Survey's tracking an ion storm. Dr. Sato says it reaches us tomorrow at two, and it's a big one.
    Farah Rahman: How big is big?
    Chief Ines Calder: Big enough that the lights flicker for two days and comms go dark. So we get ahead of it.
    Chief Ines Calder: Loose fittings secured. Shielded ballasts on the lamps that matter. Battery packs where they're needed.
    Bea Silva: The lounge bar's the worst for loose glass. Last storm we swept it up for a week.
    Chief Ines Calder: Then the lounge is yours. Somebody takes battery packs up to the bridge before the front hits.
    Chief Ines Calder: Cadet, this is your first storm. Anything you want to take on?
    [choice] I'll take the battery run to the bridge. / I'll fit the ballasts. Decks 3 and 4. / (Say nothing)
    Chief Ines Calder: Good. The packs are in main storage. Mind the lift.
    Chief Ines Calder: Right. Storm jobs are on the board. Off you go.
